  "lead_analysis": [
    "Determinism: the GP3P+Colmap repeat reproduces images.txt byte-for-byte and the full registration sequence; differences between arms are code, not noise.",
    "The faithful pull-in policy (Colmap) is best at 2.5k with GP3P (0.087 m) but worst at 5k (GP3P 0.436 m, DLT 0.699 m) versus the pre-C2.6 rule (variable points optimized on in-window observations only, no pull-in): 0.273 m at 5k.",
    "WindowOnly is a third, stricter rule (variable set ignored unless the track is fully inside) and performs badly (2.5k 1.17 m); it is not the pre-C2.6 behaviour.",
    "10k with GP3P+Colmap registers all 10000 images in one model (COLMAP: 4494+505 frames in two) but with ATE 3.27 m / scale 1.58: bridging the split that COLMAP keeps separate and the pull-in policy both need investigation.",
    "Next: restore the pre-C2.6 rule as an explicit policy, run GP3P with it at 2.5k/5k/10k, and investigate why the faithful pull-in degrades with scale (stale outside poses on revisits is the working hypothesis)."
  ]
